menu "ShrikeFi configuration"

    config SHRIKEFI_ENABLE_I2C_BITSTREAM_FLASH
        bool "Embed the ForgeFPGA bitstream and try to send it over I2C at boot"
        default n
        help
            Compiles forgefpga_bitstream.h into the firmware image and has
            shrikefi_fpga_flash_init() attempt to deliver it to the ForgeFPGA
            over I2C at power-up.

            This costs 46,408 bytes (~45 KiB) of flash. It is OFF by default
            because:

              * The Renesas SLG47910 is an FPGA, not a GreenPAK CMIC, and is not
                documented to expose a hard I2C configuration port.
              * This design's pin constraints
                (hardware/shrikefi/forgefpga_pins.pcf) declare no I2C or SPI
                configuration interface.
              * The board's FPGA is therefore expected to configure itself from
                OTP/NVM or from the onboard W25Q32JV QSPI flash at power-up.
              * The transfer itself cannot be correct for a 46 KB image anyway:
                esp32_i2c_hal_write() takes an 8-bit register address, so the
                offset wraps every 256 bytes.

            Enable this ONLY if you have confirmed that a device ACKs at
            FORGEFPGA_I2C_ADDR (0x08) -- the boot log tells you -- AND you have
            the Renesas ForgeFPGA I2C programming sequence to hand. Without that
            sequence the write is a guess.

            The 4-bit parallel link is unaffected either way: it is the runtime
            bus and never depends on this option.

endmenu
